      {
        "id": 81050,
        "name": "Envisioner",
        "username": "Envisioner",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-11-12T19:03:35.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I was right!&nbsp; I <a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/forum/topic/sneaky-vengeance-preview-in-time-cataclysm-4137\" data-bbcode=\"true\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">said</a> that at least one of the environments would be either a villain HQ or a hero HQ - and they're BOTH!&nbsp; Very excited to see Freedom Tower.</p>\n<p>But I have to ask - if you fight Baron Blade on the Mobile Defense Platform, and you destroy the Mobile Defense Platform he starts the game with, does the Environment deck go away?</p>\n<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"McBehrer\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mcbehrer/48/1850_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> McBehrer:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I'm still amazed at how thematically AWESOME the Time Cataclysm is.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Really?&nbsp; I've always thought it makes no sense at all - it's not a place where the battle is happening, but a series of events happening in different places, with no rhyme or reason connecting them.</p>",
