      {
        "id": 81055,
        "name": "Foote",
        "username": "Foote",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-11-12T20:26:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Envisioner\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Envisioner:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>but you're already inside…</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>A little imagination and abstract thought can go a long way haha</p>\n<p>(rarely do the thematics of whats happening in the card game translate into the narrative in a literal way. I played Miss Info in Pike Industral last night, her first diversion was Lab Explosion, so the narrative became that Miss Info was hiding chemical vats in the basement of the V5 HQ instead of having the heros just fight miss info at the pike complex itself. Just an example)</p>",
